   365	  // Slack (a stronger guard than a stored string — it verifies the LIVE
   366	  // credential's team), then backfill THAT team onto the row so future ticks take
   367	  // the fast/foreign-team paths above without another auth.test. We backfill the
   368	  // real team even when it isn't the one we were asked to graph: otherwise a
   369	  // connection reached first for a foreign binding would re-hit auth.test every
   370	  // tick forever. Graphing itself still requires the real team to match.
